{"id":"7f6bd20d5bf8eef791557074","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/law/2026/nov/15/uk-government-to-consider-changing-age-of-consent-after-allegations-against-russell-brand","published_at":"2026-11-15T00:17:14Z","collected_at":"2026-11-15T00:24:09.589417Z","title":"UK government to consider changing age of consent after allegations against Russell Brand","text":"British comedian and TV star Russell Brand was sentenced to 10 years and 6 months on 9 November 9, 2026 after being convicted for rape and sexual assaults, after his victims testified to the trauma they had suffered. Photograph: Brook Mitchell/AFP/Getty Images View image in fullscreen British comedian and TV star Russell Brand was sentenced to 10 years and 6 months on 9 November 9, 2026 after being convicted for rape and sexual assaults, after his victims testified to the trauma they had suffered. Photograph: Brook Mitchell/AFP/Getty Images Law UK government to consider changing age of consent after allegations against Russell Brand Deputy prime minister says change would be a massive step but ‘deserves proper consideration and scrutiny’ Raphael Boyd and Press Association Sat 14 Nov 2026 19.17 EST Last modified on Sat 14 Nov 2026 19.19 EST Share Prefer the Guardian on Google The government has said it will consider calls to change the age of consent after a woman waived her right to anonymity to publicly claim she was raped by Russell Brand as a 16-year-old schoolgirl. Mia Latter, now 37, alleged she had been orally raped by the jailed comedian when she was a teenager and he was 30","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/36adee7d1aea2fce8a66550d02c86c4385f1808c/238_0_2742_2194/master/2742.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none"],"author":"Raphael Boyd and Press Association","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha2